# Package Naming Prefixes

When adding or renaming types and exported global functions in these packages, use the package-specific prefixes below.

| Package | Type prefix | Exported global function prefix |
|---|---|---|
| `common` | `AcCm` | `accm` |
| `data-model` | `AcDb` | `acdb` |
| `geometry-engine` | `AcGe` | `acge` |
| `graphic-interface` | `AcGi` | `acgi` |

## Examples

```typescript
// ✅ common
export class AcCmColor { /* ... */ }
export function accmClamp(value: number, min: number, max: number): number { /* ... */ }

// ✅ data-model
export class AcDbLine { /* ... */ }
export function acdbOpenObject(id: string) { /* ... */ }

// ✅ geometry-engine
export class AcGePoint3d { /* ... */ }
export function acgeDistance(a: AcGePoint3d, b: AcGePoint3d): number { /* ... */ }

// ✅ graphic-interface
export interface AcGiRenderer { /* ... */ }
export function acgiCreateEntity() { /* ... */ }
```

```typescript
// ❌ Wrong package prefix
export class AcGeColor {} // in common — should be AcCmColor
export function acdbClamp() {} // in common — should be accmClamp
```

- Types include classes, interfaces, enums, and type aliases.
- Only **exported** top-level/global functions need the lowercase package prefix; private/local helpers do not.
